    <string name="faq_question_1">What should I do if I lost something on a bus?</string>
    <string name="faq_answer_1">Contact Autotrolej\'s Lost and Found office as soon as possible. Provide details about the item, the bus line, and approximate time when you lost it.</string>
    <string name="faq_question_2">How long are lost items kept?</string>
    <string name="faq_answer_2">Lost items are kept for 30 days. After that period, unclaimed items are transferred to the city\'s lost property office.</string>
    <string name="faq_question_3">What information do I need when reporting a lost item?</string>
    <string name="faq_answer_3">You should provide a detailed description of the item, the bus line number, date and time of travel, and your contact information.</string>
    <string name="faq_question_4">Can I check if my item was found online?</string>
    <string name="faq_answer_4">Currently, you need to contact the Lost and Found office directly by phone or visit in person to check if your item was found.</string>
    <string name="faq_question_5">What happens if I find someone else\'s item on the bus?</string>
    <string name="faq_answer_5">Please give it to the bus driver or bring it to the Autotrolej Lost and Found office as soon as possible.</string>
